// Linux dynamic loader bindings (libdl) (rolling).
//
// Goal:
// - Centralize the `libdl.so.2` attachment and common POSIX dlfcn symbols.
// - Used by Linux TLS provider (`std:net/tls_linux_openssl`) to lazily load OpenSSL at runtime.
//
// Notes:
// - These functions return pointers or ints in the C ABI. Oren's `ffi` defaults to i64 return,
//   which is sufficient for pointer returns on Tier‑1 x64/arm64 Linux.
// - We still attach the link dependency explicitly so the native backend emits a dynamic ELF and
//   enables `dlsym`-based resolution paths consistently.

@cfg(os="linux")
@ffi.link("libdl.so.2")
ffi { dlopen, dlsym, dlclose, dlerror }

